Original commit body from cc6f2715024e939d381dafd9976ddf1eecd62522:

WI-tinul, WI-huhin.

WI-tinul (docs only). __version__ surfaces under THREE names and the spec
named two. reproducibility_context.hypergumbo_version and
analysis_runs[].version emit it bare (7.0.0); limits.analyzer_version emits
it prefixed (hypergumbo-7.0.0). Worse, the AnalysisRun/AnalysisPass field
examples showed "hypergumbo-0.1.0" — a prefixed form the producer has never
emitted — so a consumer joining analysis_runs[].version against
limits.analyzer_version failed on a prefix the spec told them to expect on
both. The examples now show the bare emitted form, and the Version-fields
taxonomy names all three with the discriminator stated: only
analyzer_version carries the prefix, deliberately, because it is the one
surface naming the PRODUCING TOOL rather than reporting the version of a
record the tool already authored. No emitted value changed.

WI-huhin (consumer-visible value change). confidence_model emitted
"hypergumbo-evidence-v2" against a documented grammar of
hypergumbo-evidence-vMAJOR.MINOR (Appendix C), which assigns MINOR the job
"Refinements (new evidence types, score adjustments)". A bare MAJOR makes
that channel unexpressible — ADR-0039's refinement added evidence types,
exactly what MINOR signals, and had no way to say so; the next refinement
would have had to choose between a misleading MAJOR bump and silence.

The field now emits "hypergumbo-evidence-v2.0": the first CONFORMING
rendering of the SAME model. MAJOR unchanged, no scoring behaviour differs,
and the spec now says so explicitly so v2.0 is not misread as a refinement
of v2. The value was fixed rather than the grammar because the grammar is a
considered taxonomy defining MAJOR/MINOR across three version families
while the bare constant is one nobody revisited — reconcile toward the
artifact carrying the decision. Blast radius: one producer constant, two
assertions, swept for stragglers.

test_confidence_model_matches_documented_grammar pins the FORMAT, not the
literal, so a legitimate future bump passes and only a malformed value
fails. 2011 passed across the 45-file affected set.

